@startuml paired_consent_rotation
title Paired consent rotation and persistent duress delivery
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 100

actor User as U
participant "Iso signer" as I
participant "Relay host" as H
participant "Secure Terminal" as S
participant "Boomlet source" as B
participant "Boomletwo inactive" as W
participant "Watchtower" as T
participant "Setup-bound SAR" as A

note over S,W
  PairBinding and its normal-key certificate are provisioned and retained.
  Source and target have separate management keys; the logical peer key is copied.
  ST retains its logical Boomlet pairing, setup ID, normal key, pair digest and generation.
  Both consent records and prior decision floors match before a new attempt.
  No withdrawal, signing handoff, outstanding check, or SAR duty may be unresolved.
end note

note over H,W
  ENC = SPEC cbc_cmac_encrypt; DEC authenticates before decryption.
  SIG = SPEC sign_message; VERIFY checks exact signer, domain and content type.
  DOM(op) = "Boomerang/consent_rotation/v1/" + fixed_operation.
  CTX(op) = canonical_encode("consent_rotation_" + fixed_operation, setup_id).
  LCTX(op) = canonical_encode("consent_rotation_" + fixed_ST_operation).
  E_BW(op,P) = ENC(k_BW, CTX(op), SIG(B_management, DOM(op), P)).
  E_WB(op,P) = ENC(k_WB, CTX(op), SIG(W_management, DOM(op), P)).
  k_BW and k_WB use certified physical keys, roles, direction and PROTOCOL_VERSION.
  ST encryption uses the existing directional logical Boomlet/ST keys.
  EH(E) = sha256(canonical_encode(E)); CD(C) hashes the canonical Candidate.
  Frame(op,E) uses the fixed selector, u16 envelope length and zero transport padding.
  Every fresh envelope uses a fresh IV. Retries preserve exact bytes.
end note

note over B,W
  Every receive checks bounded framing, expected context, canonical payload,
  exact scope, authorized sender, operation, attempt floor and journal phase.
  Invalid input preserves authority holds and duress; failures are uniform.
  Every response uses a trusted receipt-relative fixed release deadline.
  Durable state and exact reply are stored before release.
  The relay only copies bytes and supplies no authority or trusted timing.
end note

group Trusted review and normal-key authorization
  U -> I: Request consent replacement; reconstruct normal key
  I -> H: BEGIN_REVIEW, empty canonical tuple
  H -> B: BEGIN_REVIEW
  B -> B: Check current binding, resolved predecessor and bounded capacity
  B -> B: Create Scope with next attempt_seq, fresh rotation_id and new_commit_id
  B -> B: Create review_nonce; retain one volatile pending intent
  B -> B: Review = MessageWithNonce(Scope, review_nonce)
  B -> B: E_review = ENC(k_BS, LCTX(review_challenge), (PairCertificate, Review))
  B -> H: (PairCertificate, Scope, E_review)
  H -> I: Public PairCertificate and Scope
  H -> S: Frame(review_challenge, E_review)
  S -> S: DEC; verify normal certificate, stored anchors, logical pairing and Scope
  S -> U: Display consent replacement, setup, device pair and epochs
  U -> S: Approve exact intent
  S -> S: A_st = SIG(ST, DOM(st_review), Review)
  S -> S: E_review_approval = ENC(k_SB, LCTX(review_approval), A_st)
  S -> H: Frame(review_approval, E_review_approval)
  H -> B: SUBMIT_REVIEW(E_review_approval)
  B -> B: DEC; VERIFY A_st; require pending Scope and review_nonce
  B -> H: Verified A_st, containing no countries or duress state
  H -> I: A_st
  I -> I: Verify recovered normal key, pair certificate, ST signature and exact Scope
  I -> I: Auth = SIG(normal_key, DOM(authorize), A_st)
  I -> H: SUBMIT_AUTH(Auth)
  H -> B: SUBMIT_AUTH(Auth)
  B -> B: Verify Auth and A_st against pending intent and stored normal/ST keys
  B -> B: Atomically reserve journal, set attempt floor, quarantine predecessor, enter HOLD_WAIT
end

group Both devices held before the previous-set question
  B -> B: P_hold = (Scope, PairCertificate, Auth)
  B -> B: Store E_hold = E_BW(hold, P_hold) before output
  B -> H: Frame(hold, E_hold)
  H -> W: Exact frame
  W -> W: DEC; VERIFY source management signature, normal Auth and ST review
  W -> W: Require inactive role, binding, next attempt_seq and matching predecessor/floors
  W -> W: Atomically reserve journal, quarantine predecessor and enter HELD
  W -> W: Store E_held = E_WB(held, (Scope, EH(E_hold), base_state_seq, D_W))
  W -> H: Frame(held, E_held), at fixed release deadline
  H -> B: Exact frame

  alt HELD is authenticated and durably consumed
    B -> B: DEC; VERIFY target signature, EH(E_hold), Scope and base sequence
    B -> B: Atomically record HELD and D_B = D_B OR D_W
    B -> B: Create n_prev and permutation of 1..193; enter PREVIOUS_PENDING
    B -> B: Q_prev = MessageWithNonce(Check(Scope, 0, 1, space_prev), n_prev)
    B -> B: Store challenge and E_prev = ENC(k_BS, LCTX(previous_challenge), Q_prev)
    B -> H: Frame(previous_challenge, E_prev)
    H -> S: Exact frame
    S -> S: DEC; validate Scope/round/phase and build five independent display maps
    S -> U: Ask for previous committed set without displaying the answer
    U -> S: Select five distinct countries
    S -> S: R_prev = MessageWithNonce(Answer(Scope, 0, 1, original_indices), n_prev)
    S -> H: Frame(previous_answer, ENC(k_SB, LCTX(previous_answer), R_prev))
    H -> B: Exact frame
    B -> B: DEC; check outstanding scope/phase/nonce, five distinct indices and ranges
    B -> B: Resolve countries; compare all five against committed predecessor
    B -> B: D_B = D_B OR mismatch; answer_seq = base_state_seq + 1
    B -> B: E_continue = ENC(k_BS, LCTX(previous_result), MessageWithNonce(UiResult(Scope,0,0),n_prev))
    B -> B: Atomically consume response, persist D_B/answer_seq/cache and enter ENROLLING
    B -> H: Frame(previous_result, E_continue), at fixed release deadline
    H -> S: Exact frame
    S -> S: DEC; verify expected Scope and n_prev; continue without correctness feedback

    loop Enrollment round r = 1..3 until READY or cancellation
      B -> B: Create n_select and fresh space; persist outstanding phase 2
      B -> B: Q_select = MessageWithNonce(Check(Scope,r,2,space_select),n_select)
      B -> H: Frame(selection_challenge, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(selection_challenge),Q_select))
      H -> S: Exact frame
      S -> S: DEC; require Scope/r/phase 2; replace display maps
      S -> U: Choose fresh set
      U -> S: Select five distinct countries
      S -> S: R_select = MessageWithNonce(Answer(Scope,r,2,indices),n_select)
      S -> H: Frame(selection_answer, ENC(k_SB,LCTX(selection_answer),R_select))
      H -> B: Exact frame
      B -> B: DEC; validate nonce/count/ranges; resolve and journal candidate selection
      B -> B: Compute history non-reuse without changing D_B

      B -> B: Create n_confirm1 and fresh space; persist outstanding phase 3
      B -> B: Q1 = MessageWithNonce(Check(Scope,r,3,space1),n_confirm1)
      B -> H: Frame(confirmation_1_challenge, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(confirmation_1_challenge),Q1))
      H -> S: Exact frame
      S -> S: DEC; require Scope/r/phase 3; replace display maps
      S -> U: Reproduce the candidate set
      U -> S: Select five distinct countries
      S -> S: R1 = MessageWithNonce(Answer(Scope,r,3,indices),n_confirm1)
      S -> H: Frame(confirmation_1_answer, ENC(k_SB,LCTX(confirmation_1_answer),R1))
      H -> B: Exact frame
      B -> B: DEC; validate and consume; record first comparison, preserving D_B

      B -> B: Create n_confirm2 and fresh space; persist outstanding phase 4
      B -> B: Q2 = MessageWithNonce(Check(Scope,r,4,space2),n_confirm2)
      B -> H: Frame(confirmation_2_challenge, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(confirmation_2_challenge),Q2))
      H -> S: Exact frame
      S -> S: DEC; require Scope/r/phase 4; replace display maps
      S -> U: Reproduce the candidate set
      U -> S: Select five distinct countries
      S -> S: R2 = MessageWithNonce(Answer(Scope,r,4,indices),n_confirm2)
      S -> H: Frame(confirmation_2_answer, ENC(k_SB,LCTX(confirmation_2_answer),R2))
      H -> B: Exact frame
      B -> B: DEC; validate and consume; record second comparison, preserving D_B
      B -> B: result = READY(2) iff valid, unused, and both confirmations match; otherwise RETRY(1)
      B -> B: Cache E_round = ENC(k_BS,LCTX(round_result),MessageWithNonce(UiResult(Scope,r,result),n_confirm2))
      B -> H: Frame(round_result, E_round), at fixed release deadline
      H -> S: Exact frame
      S -> S: DEC; verify Scope/r/n_confirm2 and display candidate result only
    end

    opt Authenticated cancellation, applicable at any precommit ST phase
      U -> H: REQUEST_CANCEL
      H -> B: REQUEST_CANCEL, empty canonical tuple
      B -> B: Serialize with acceptance; retire pending country challenge; preserve accepted duress
      B -> B: Store fresh cancel_nonce and Q_cancel = MessageWithNonce(Scope,cancel_nonce)
      B -> H: Frame(cancel_challenge, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(cancel_challenge),Q_cancel))
      H -> S: Exact frame
      S -> S: DEC; verify active Scope and nonce
      S -> U: Confirm cancellation
      U -> S: Approve cancellation
      S -> S: A_cancel = SIG(ST,DOM(st_cancel),Q_cancel)
      S -> H: Frame(cancel_approval,ENC(k_SB,LCTX(cancel_approval),A_cancel))
      H -> B: Exact frame
      B -> B: DEC; VERIFY ST signature, Scope and cancel_nonce; atomically consume and record cancelled
    end

    alt Candidate READY and not cancelled
      B -> B: C = (Scope,new_set,count+1,32 padded history rows,base+1,base+2,D_B)
      B -> B: Freeze enrollment and competing operations
      B -> B: Atomically store C and E_prepare = E_BW(prepare,(C)); enter PREPARE_WAIT
      B -> H: Frame(prepare, E_prepare)
      H -> W: Exact frame
      W -> W: DEC; VERIFY source signature; require HELD and matching authorization/Scope
      W -> W: Check complete history prefix, appended new set, non-reuse and sequences
      W -> W: C_star = C with latch D_W OR C.duress_latched
      W -> W: E_prepared = E_WB(prepared,(Scope,EH(E_prepare),C_star))
      W -> W: Atomically persist D_W, answer_seq, C_star, E_prepared; enter PREPARED
      W -> H: Frame(prepared, E_prepared), at fixed release deadline
      H -> B: Exact frame
      B -> B: DEC; VERIFY target signature, EH(E_prepare) and all candidate fields
      B -> B: Permit only OR latch merge; atomically persist C_star and receipt; enter PREPARED
    else Candidate unavailable, third round failed, or cancellation accepted
      B -> B: Keep accepted D_B and quarantine; no commit readiness
    end

    alt Both durable prepares exist and coordinator chooses COMMIT
      B -> B: E_commit = E_BW(commit,(Scope,EH(E_prepared),CD(C_star),base+2))
      B -> B: Atomically install C_star, final sequence, COMMIT decision and exact bytes; enter COMMIT_WAIT
      B -> H: Frame(commit, E_commit)
      H -> W: Exact frame
      W -> W: DEC; VERIFY source signature; match EH(E_prepared), CD(C_star), final sequence
      W -> W: E_committed = E_WB(committed,(Scope,EH(E_commit),CD(C_star),base+2,D_W))
      W -> W: Atomically install C_star and receipt; enter COMPLETE, still inactive
      W -> H: Frame(committed, E_committed), at fixed release deadline
      H -> B: Exact frame
      B -> B: DEC; VERIFY Scope, EH(E_commit), CD(C_star), sequence and prepared latch
      B -> B: Atomically retain terminal evidence; clear withdrawal quarantine; enter COMPLETE
      B -> H: Frame(terminal_result, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(terminal_result),MessageWithNonce(UiResult(Scope,r,3),ui_anchor)))
      H -> S: Exact frame
      S -> S: DEC; match active Scope/ui_anchor; display completion once
    else Coordinator chooses ABORT before any durable COMMIT
      B -> B: checked = journal.has_accepted_previous; final_seq = base + 1 + checked
      B -> B: E_abort = E_BW(abort,(Scope,checked,final_seq,D_B))
      B -> B: Atomically record ABORT decision, final sequence and exact bytes; enter ABORT_WAIT
      B -> H: Frame(abort, E_abort)
      H -> W: Exact frame
      W -> W: DEC; VERIFY source signature; require HELD or PREPARED, matching Scope and final sequence
      W -> W: D_W = D_W OR received_latch; E_aborted = E_WB(aborted,(Scope,EH(E_abort),final_seq,D_W))
      W -> W: Atomically retain D_W, quarantine, sequence, attempt floor and exact receipt; enter ABORTED
      W -> H: Frame(aborted, E_aborted), at fixed release deadline
      H -> B: Exact frame
      B -> B: DEC; VERIFY exact request digest/sequence; persist OR merge and terminal receipt; enter ABORTED
      B -> B: Preserve predecessor quarantine; discard only staged candidate material
      B -> H: Frame(terminal_result, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(terminal_result),MessageWithNonce(UiResult(Scope,r,4),ui_anchor)))
      H -> S: Exact frame
      S -> S: DEC; match Scope/ui_anchor; display cancellation without duress classification
    end

  else HELD is unavailable or unacknowledged
    B -> B: No previous-set question is issued; previous_checked is false
    B -> B: E_abort0 = E_BW(abort_unheld,(Scope,PairCertificate,Auth,base+1,D_B))
    B -> B: Atomically record ABORT decision, final sequence and exact bytes; enter ABORT_WAIT
    B -> H: Frame(abort_unheld, E_abort0)
    H -> W: Exact frame, even if the earlier HOLD was lost
    W -> W: DEC; VERIFY source signature, normal authorization, ST review, binding and attempt floor
    W -> W: Require unseen or HELD; preserve quarantine; D_W = D_W OR received_latch
    W -> W: Atomically record ABORTED, base+1, floor and E_aborted0 = E_WB(aborted,(Scope,EH(E_abort0),base+1,D_W))
    W -> H: Frame(aborted, E_aborted0), at fixed release deadline
    H -> B: Exact frame
    B -> B: DEC; VERIFY Scope/EH(E_abort0)/sequence; persist OR merge and terminal evidence
    B -> H: Frame(terminal_result, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(terminal_result),MessageWithNonce(UiResult(Scope,0,4),review_nonce)))
    H -> S: Exact frame
    S -> S: DEC; verify reviewed Scope and review_nonce; display cancellation once
  end
end

group Recovery at any interrupted control boundary
  opt Delivery retry while the bound attempt remains admitted
    B -> H: Retransmit exact stored Frame(op,E_request)
    H -> W: Exact bytes, without a new IV or altered candidate
    W -> W: Match accepted request digest; no repeated state transition or persistent write
    W -> H: Exact cached receipt, released on this delivery's fixed deadline
    H -> B: Exact bytes
    B -> B: Consume idempotently only in the proper decision/receipt handler
  end

  opt Source needs current target evidence
    B -> B: Reserve query slot; generate fresh query_nonce; store E_query = E_BW(status,(Scope,query_nonce))
    B -> H: Frame(status, E_query)
    H -> W: Exact frame
    W -> W: DEC; VERIFY bound attempt and query budget; read durable phase/sequence and terminal evidence
    W -> W: Store E_status = E_WB(status_response,(Scope,EH(E_query),query_nonce,phase,seq,kind,evidence_bytes))
    W -> H: Frame(status_response, E_status), at fixed release deadline
    H -> B: Exact frame
    B -> B: DEC; VERIFY Scope, request digest, fresh query nonce and bounded evidence
    B -> B: Apply terminal evidence and its latch merge through the exact decision/receipt handler
    note over B,W
      PREPARED without a source decision cannot activate the backup.
      Resend exact PREPARE to recover PREPARED; STATUS creates no decision.
      Recover COMMITTED or ABORTED through their normal receipt handlers.
      A source already at COMMIT_WAIT must finish COMMIT, never abort.
    end note
  end

  opt Prepared target needs the source decision
    W -> W: Reserve query slot; generate fresh target_query_nonce; store E_query2 = E_WB(status,(Scope,target_query_nonce))
    W -> H: Frame(status, E_query2)
    H -> B: Exact frame
    B -> B: DEC; VERIFY current attempt and nonce; select exact durable decision or NONE
    B -> B: Check query budget; store E_status2 = E_BW(status_response,(Scope,EH(E_query2),target_query_nonce,phase,seq,kind,evidence_bytes))
    B -> H: Frame(status_response, E_status2), at fixed release deadline
    H -> W: Exact frame
    W -> W: DEC; VERIFY fresh nonce and scope; recover original COMMIT/ABORT envelope through its handler
    note over B,W
      NONE, timeout, missing source, or conflicting evidence leaves authority held.
      No old receipt reconstructs an untransferred latch or proves current eligibility.
    end note
  end
end

group ST restart or terminal-result loss
  S -> S: Create fresh ui_query_nonce using retained setup and pair anchors
  S -> H: Frame(ui_status,ENC(k_SB,LCTX(ui_status),MessageWithNonce((setup_id,pair_digest),ui_query_nonce)))
  H -> B: Exact frame
  B -> B: DEC; match retained binding; check eight-query budget; read current or last terminal journal
  B -> B: Retire any unconsumed input nonce; prepare fresh UiResume; preserve accepted duress
  B -> B: Pending cancellation uses phase 5, fresh cancel nonce and identity-space padding
  B -> B: E_ui_reply = ENC(k_BS,LCTX(ui_status_response),MessageWithNonce((Scope,ui_status,UiResume),ui_query_nonce))
  B -> B: Atomically store replacement, query acceptance and exact E_ui_reply
  B -> H: Frame(ui_status_response,E_ui_reply)
  H -> S: Exact frame
  S -> S: DEC; verify its outstanding query nonce and Scope; use only the authenticated UiResume after restart
  S -> S: Display terminal status once, rebuild country maps, or confirm the resumed cancellation
  note over S,W
    Eight fresh STATUS queries per direction and eight UI queries are reserved per attempt.
    Exact duplicate queries recover cached bytes without writes or nonce replacement.
    Exhaustion stalls fresh queries and preserves decisions, holds and duress.
  end note
end

group Subsequent ordinary withdrawal after rotation completion
  note over S,A
    The eligible active device is B, or W after independently proved activation.
    Transaction review, unanimous approvals, digging and signing rules still apply.
    This subflow shows the existing local placeholder path for initial commit and every Ping.
  end note

  loop Initial TxCommit, then every new Ping
    B -> B: effective_duress = retained_duress_latched OR current_check_is_duress
    B -> B: p = doxing_key_for_sar if effective_duress, otherwise zero_bytes_32
    B -> B: P = ENC(k_BSAR,canonical_encode("withdrawal_duress_placeholder",approved_id),p), fresh IV
    B -> B: inner = SIG(logical_Boomlet,"Boomerang/withdrawal/" + kind, TxCommit_or_Ping)
    B -> B: outer = SIG(logical_Boomlet,"Boomerang/withdrawal/" + kind + "_envelope",PaddedMessage(inner,P))
    B -> H: ENC(k_BWT,canonical_encode("withdrawal_" + kind,approved_id),outer)
    H -> T: Exact withdrawal envelope
    T -> T: DEC; verify both signatures, approval/commit gate, approved ID and freshness/sequence
    T -> A: Exact P on existing setup-bound placeholder forwarding path
    A -> A: Set fixed ack_release_at before parsing; authenticate, decrypt and classify P
    A -> A: Construct signed exact-envelope acknowledgment and identical fixed-shape processing record
    A -> A: Durably commit replay tuple (approved_id,logical_Boomlet_pubkey,P.iv); activate duress for new valid duress tuple
    A -> A: Ack = SIG(SAR,"Boomerang/withdrawal/sar_placeholder_response",P)
    A -> A: E_ack = ENC(k_SARB,canonical_encode("withdrawal_sar_placeholder_response",approved_id),Ack)
    A -> T: Exact E_ack at the fixed deadline; no late acknowledgment after overrun
    T -> H: E_ack with existing verified commit collection or encrypted Pong
    H -> B: Exact withdrawal delivery
    B -> B: DEC E_ack; verify SAR signature and byte-for-byte Ack.content == P
    B -> B: Verify accompanying withdrawal evidence before any progress
  end

  note over B,A
    Correct answers to the new set cannot override a true persistent latch.
    Every new Ping uses a new placeholder IV; in-flight retries retain exact bytes.
    Safe and duress share message shape, timing, queues, writes, retries and exposed status.
    Rescue work cannot change acknowledgment release or reveal classification to the relay.
    No later traffic means no delivery claim, even though the latch remains durable.
  end note
end
@enduml
